== Games

Most of the inspiration behind this research came from the games we enjoy.

=== Terraria
_Living Trees_ in _Terraria_ #footnote[https://www.terraria.org/] 
are structures that spawn on the surface and in underground jungles. 
Players enjoy building bases around or inside such trees, 
to the point of the developers increasing the likelyhood of 
trees spawning next to eachother, for players to build overhang treehouses
#footnote[https://terraria.wiki.gg/wiki/Living_Tree#History].

=== @MC:lo
Vanilla @MC is not very creative when it comes to big trees,
the best we have are tall jungle and spruce trees.
There are plenty of player builds of treehouses and such out there,
but we want to bring up a fun mod instead. 

The original mod is not maintained anymore, but a standalone 
is available #footnote[https://github.com/Blue-Beaker/Sacred-Trees],
where trees can span multiple _regions_ of _chunks_.
Mods are also convenient because we can look at their code and see how 
large trees or structures are generated in practice,
giving us a glimpse into upsides and pitfalls.